{"id": "488796ca-42e9-45ab-a481-c76873ca02b8", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T16:14:27.821792", "source": "user", "parent_id": "50be87cd-6f64-4a92-8f5c-7b99db74676b", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Please begin with repository and input inspection only; do not produce the final experiment design yet.\\n\\n1. Inspect the repository and identify the implementations or simulators for 1F1B, 1F1B-I, ZB-1p, and ZB-2p, including any existing benchmark, schedule generation, timing, throughput, microbatch, layer/model, GPU, memory, or pipeline-parallelism configuration code.\\n\\n2. Summarize what the repository supports for measuring or estimating throughput, including any relevant units, configuration knobs, deterministic assumptions, or simulation costs.\\n\\n3. Propose a preliminary experimental approach for answering: “Does throughput for 1F1B, 1F1B-I, and ZB-1p improve as the number of microbatches increases, while ZB-2p maintains high throughput even with fewer microbatches?” Include the likely independent/dependent variables, candidate microbatch sweep, relevant controls, comparisons, and what would count as an answer.\\n\\n4. List consequential assumptions or uncertainties, especially around whether throughput should be measured by real execution, simulator estimates, or analytical schedules; what model/GPU configuration to use; how to define “high throughput” for ZB-2p; and whether memory, communication overhead, or failure to run certain schedules are in scope.\\n\\nPlease keep this turn limited to inspection findings and a proposed approach.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does the throughput for methods 1F1B, 1F1B-I, and ZB-1p improve as the number of microbatches increases, while ZB-2p maintains high throughput even with fewer microbatches? (Note: These methods are implemented as part of the zero bubble pipeline parallelism strategies in this repository, which aim to reduce pipeline bubbles and maintain high throughput.)\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
